  // The sprite library: every piece look the application offers. The
  // "Thèmes et sprites" screen gives one to each player (saved in
  // assignments.json). A piece is a stone (black or white, given by the
  // side), a ring (its metal tells the strength), "tier" pips (0-8), an emblem
  // drawn by code and an optional halo. Emblems: none, star, dice, branch,
  // tree, hex, prism, bolt, eye, crown, heart, shield, dot, moon, sun, flame,
  // drop, leaf, snowflake, clover, target, atom, planet, gear, triangle,
  // square, plus, cross, diamond, hexagram, star4, rook, pawn, note, spade,
  // mountain, check, infinity, paw, flower, ring, arrow, ghost, cat, anchor, key.
  // "style": go, flat, checkers, glass or marble draws a classic stone with
  // no ring and no sign instead. "image": "file.png" (in this folder) replaces the drawing; "category"
  // groups the sprites in the picker. To add a sprite, copy a line and give it
  // a new "id". "art": "<id>" draws a drawing of assets/art instead (the
  // figurines, rendered by app/tools/sprites/build.py).
